cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "options-pricing-engine"
abstract: >-
  A C++20 options pricing library providing Black-Scholes-Merton closed-form
  prices and Greeks, Cox-Ross-Rubinstein binomial lattices, Monte Carlo with
  variance reduction, Longstaff-Schwartz least-squares Monte Carlo for American
  exercise, and implied-volatility inversion against real option chains.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Lie"
    given-names: "Lyonn"
    alias: "leeyawnnn"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leeyawnnn/options-pricing-engine"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - options-pricing
  - black-scholes
  - monte-carlo
  - implied-volatility
  - quantitative-finance
  - cpp20
